    "description": "Read one delivery offer in any state (QUOTED, EXPIRED or CONSUMED): its tier, groupNo, destination postal prefix, lines, delivery window (earliest, latest and the delivery station's IANA timeZone, the local calendar of its days), the witness path that proves feasibility (node, pickup departure, legs, delivery wave), basis (SCHEDULED from the timetable, MEASURED when a leg's measured transit pushed the arrival later, or NOMINAL lane times), the optional confidence (0 to 1: the calibrated probability that the quote is kept on time, absent when the service has too few judgements of its segment to say, which is unknown and not zero), the policyVersion it was quoted under, quotedAt/expiresAt, and orderByAt (the latest instant the order can be placed and still make the quoted window, uncapped by the offer TTL). Offers are kept for a retention period after they expire. Read-only; an unknown offer fails with not-found.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "offerId": {
          "description": "the delivery offer id returned by quote, e.g. off-1",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "offerId"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "name": "get_delivery_offer",
    "outputSchema": {
